sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.5}{1-0.6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.5}{0.4} \\\\  & =6.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538999 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538999 #edb/ref 1069 "q-353150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538999 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538999 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n9.6-0.96+0.096-0.0096+⋯.\n$$\n\n Do not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538999 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2fe4d85-a3ec-5968-ad10-7f316b6ab6b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538999 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=9.6$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-0.96}{9.6}=-0.1.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{9.6}{1-(-0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9.6}{1+0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9.6}{1.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{960}{110} \\\\  & =\\frac{96}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539047 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186539109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539047 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2523b52f-6ffd-5128-a11b-bfb54528d1ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539047 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186538997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539076 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186539047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539076 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a955af1-f546-5512-be6c-5091a7427f58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539076 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186538981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539086 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 175921865